  {
   "evidence": "`grep -n '\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 (innerSL|euclidean)' code/TauCeti` hits only PoincareMetric.lean:98; the only other metric-scaling in the repo is the new `conformal` (Conformal.lean:40-71). The needed instances (`FiberBundle`/`VectorBundle` on `fun z : \u210d \u21a6 TangentSpace \ud835\udcd8(\u211d, \u2102) z`) are available from `instIsManifoldReal` (PoincareMetric.lean:33), which the file already relies on for `contMDiffAt_section`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Complex/UpperHalfPlane/PoincareMetric.lean",
   "fix": "Split the Poincar\u00e9 metric: keep the flat part as an auxiliary `ContMDiffRiemannianMetric \ud835\udcd8(\u211d, \u2102) \u221e \u2102 (fun z : \u210d \u21a6 TangentSpace \ud835\udcd8(\u211d, \u2102) z)` with `inner z := arrowCongr \u2026 innerSL` (trivial `symm`/`pos`/`isVonNBounded`, and the existing `contMDiff` convert-block with `hconst` in place of the scaled section), then set `poincareRiemannianMetric := flat.conformal (fun z : \u210d \u21a6 (z.im ^ 2)\u207b\u00b9) h hpos`, where `h` comes from the existing `him` and `hpos` from `z.im_pos`. `poincareRiemannianMetric_inner` then follows from `conformal_inner` as `riemannianMetric_inner` does in the new file.",
   "issue": "`poincareRiemannianMetric` is a near-clone of the construction this PR adds: its `inner` is `(z.im ^ 2)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 innerSL` (line 57) and its `symm` (60), `pos` (66, `mul_pos (inv_pos.mpr ...) ...`), `isVonNBounded` (71, rescaling the unit ball by `z.im`) and `contMDiff` (97-99, `((him.pow 2).inv\u2080 _).smul hconst`) fields are all exactly the scalar-factor bookkeeping that `Bundle.ContMDiffRiemannianMetric.conformal` now discharges once and for all. After this PR there are two independent implementations of \"multiply a C^n metric by a positive C^n function\".",
   "line": 51
  },
  {
   "evidence": "UpperHalfSpace.lean:200-208 vs 237-243; `inner_def := riemannianMetric_inner x v w` type-checks only because the two propositions are definitionally equal.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Riemannian/Hyperbolic/UpperHalfSpace.lean",
   "fix": "Keep one: inline the `conformal_inner`/`euclideanMetric_inner`/`div_eq_inv_mul` proof into `inner_def`, mark `inner_def` `@[simp]`, and delete `riemannianMetric_inner` (nothing else in the file uses it except `inner_def`).",
   "issue": "`riemannianMetric_inner` (simp) and `inner_def` state the same equation up to defeq \u2014 the `RiemannianBundle` instance is `\u27e8riemannianMetric.toRiemannianMetric\u27e9`, so `inner \u211d v w` and `riemannianMetric.inner x v w` have identical RHS and `inner_def`'s proof is the bare term `riemannianMetric_inner x v w` with no conversion step. Two public names for one fact.",
   "line": 202
  }
 ],
